Input: {"question": "In which significant event was User authentication using video analysis involved?", "documents": [{"doc_id": "d1", "text": "As the sun set over the bustling streets of Tokyo, the anticipation was palpable. The city was abuzz with excitement, for tonight was the night of the most anticipated event of the year - the grand finale of the prestigious \"Tokyo Dreams\" talent show. The iconic Shibuya Crossing was transformed into a sea of glittering lights and giant screens, as thousands of fans gathered to witness the crowning of the next big star. Behind the scenes, the production team was working tirelessly to ensure a seamless and secure experience for the performers, judges, and audience alike. Amidst the chaos, a quiet revolution was taking place. Unbeknownst to the cheering crowds, the event's organizers had partnered with a cutting-edge tech firm to introduce a game-changing innovation - user authentication using video analysis. In a cramped, dimly lit control room, a team of experts from NeuroSpark Technologies huddled around a bank of monitors, their eyes fixed on the real-time feeds from the venue. Led by the enigmatic and brilliant Dr. Rachel Kim, they had spent months perfecting their proprietary AI-powered system, designed to verify the identities of performers, crew members, and VIP guests using subtle patterns in their facial expressions, body language, and micro-movements. As the show's host, the charismatic Taro Yamada, took the stage to introduce the final act, the NeuroSpark team sprang into action. Discreetly positioned cameras captured the performers' every move, transmitting the footage to the control room for analysis. In a matter of seconds, the AI system, dubbed \"Echo,\" would verify their identities, ensuring that only authorized individuals had access to the stage and sensitive areas. Meanwhile, in the wings, contestant Akira Matsumoto was preparing to perform the routine of a lifetime. As she took a deep breath, a tiny, al